<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1"><strong>=F0=9F=8C=B1 N=
gu=E1=BB=93n G=E1=BB=91c &amp; Motivation</strong></h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Problem Statement Chi Ti=
=E1=BA=BFt:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Red envelope distribution (=E5=
=BE=AE=E4=BF=A1=E7=BA=A2=E5=8C=85=E7=AE=97=E6=B3=95) is a classic computer =
science problem disguised as social feature. Core challenge l=C3=A0 distrib=
ute a fixed amount fairly among N people with constraints:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Fairness</strong>: Ever=
yone gets reasonable amount (not too skewed)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Randomness</strong>: Un=
predictable distribution creates excitement</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Minimum Guarantee</stro=
ng>: Everyone gets at least minimum amount (usually 1 cent)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Sum Preservation</stron=
g>: Total distributed exactly equals original amount</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Real-time Performance</=
