<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">=F0=9F=92=AD <strong>Debugging M=
ental Model</strong>: <em>When red envelope distribution seems unfair, I ch=
eck: 1) Input validation (negative amounts, edge cases), 2) Randomness qual=
ity (seed consistency for testing), 3) Constraint violations (minimums, max=
imums), 4) Statistical analysis (skewness, variance), 5) Edge case handling=
 (single person, equal amounts).</em></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Common Interview Questio=
ns:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Q: Why not just divide e=
qually?</strong>
<strong>A</strong>: Equal division removes randomness element, which reduce=
s engagement. Random distribution creates excitement v=C3=A0 anticipation, =
driving user engagement.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Q: How do you ensure fai=
rness trong random distribution?</strong>
<strong>A</strong>: Use bounded randomness (double average method), enforce=
 minimums, limit maximum skewness, v=C3=A0 provide statistical analysis for=
 audit.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Q: What's time complexit=
y c=E1=BB=A7a double average method?</strong>
<strong>A</strong>: O(n) time, O(1) extra space. Linear iteration with cons=
tant work per person.</p>
