<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">=F0=9F=92=AD <strong>Debugging M=
ental Model</strong>: <em>When timing seems off, I debug systematically: 1)=
 Check browser throttling (background tabs), 2) Measure actual vs expected =
intervals, 3) Look for blocking operations, 4) Test drift accumulation over=
 time, 5) Verify cleanup on stop.</em></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Common Interview Questio=
ns:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Q: Why is chained setTim=
eout better than setInterval?</strong>
<strong>A</strong>: Chained setTimeout prevents execution overlap, allows d=
ynamic interval adjustment, provides better error isolation, v=C3=A0 enable=
s drift correction.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Q: How do you handle pre=
cision timing trong JavaScript?</strong>
<strong>A</strong>: Use performance.now() for measurements, requestAnimatio=
nFrame cho visual sync, Web Workers for background precision, v=C3=A0 imple=
ment drift correction algorithms.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Q: What happens if callb=
ack execution takes longer than interval?</strong>
<strong>A</strong>:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>setInterval</strong>: N=
ext execution queues immediately, causing rapid firing</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>chained setTimeout</str=
ong>: Next execution waits for current to complete, preventing overlap</li>
</ul>
